      "title": "First Australian death of little penguin with H5 bird flu confirmed on Phillip Island",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/15/little-penguin-found-dead-with-h5-bird-flu-on-victorias-phillip-island",
      "description": "<p>Authorities confirm first Australian death of species found with virus near where it attracts crowds to a ‘penguin parade’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s first case of the deadly H5 bird flu in a little penguin has been confirmed on Victoria’s Phillip Island, only days after the state government announced it would begin vaccinating the species.</p><p>Confirmation of the virus in the little penguin will spark a race to vaccinate thousands of birds, with the government announcing on Saturday it would begin the rollout on Monday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/15/little-penguin-found-dead-with-h5-bird-flu-on-victorias-phillip-island\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-15T07:01:50"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘My heart breaks into a million pieces’: emotional tributes to Kumanjayi Little Baby at Alice Springs funeral",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/15/emotional-tributes-kumanjayi-little-baby-alice-springs-funeral-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Hundreds gathered with flashes of pink to farewell the five-year-old girl, who was allegedly murdered in April</p><ul><li><p><em><strong>Warning: </strong>This story contains references to Indigenous Australians who have died</em></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A sombre funeral service for Kumanjayi Little Baby has been attended by hundreds of people from the Alice Springs community and surrounds.</p><p>Wearing pink and some dressed in T-shirts bearing the face of the five-year-old girl, the crowd gathered under grey skies in the red centre capital on Saturday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/15/emotional-tributes-kumanjayi-little-baby-alice-springs-funeral-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-15T04:58:20"
    },
    {
      "title": "Coalition split on Andrew Bragg speech as South Australian senator Andrew McLachlan urges colleagues to ‘follow his lead’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/15/coalition-split-on-andrew-bragg-speech-as-south-australian-senator-andrew-mclachlan-urges-colleagues-to-follow-his-lead",
      "description": "<p>Senior colleagues dismiss Bragg’s migration figures as ‘personal views’ while others say critical response is an ‘overreaction’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Liberal senator Andrew McLachlan has publicly backed Andrew Bragg and urged colleagues to “follow his lead” after a public speech that has split colleagues and triggered a rebuke from the opposition leader, Angus Taylor.</p><p>At the National Press Club on Wednesday, Bragg announced a policy to slash the national construction code and suggested net overseas migration should be dropped from the current level of about 300,000 to below 180,000 a year to keep pace with new housing builds.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/15/coalition-split-on-andrew-bragg-speech-as-south-australian-senator-andrew-mclachlan-urges-colleagues-to-follow-his-lead\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-15T02:00:43"
    },
    {
      "title": "Fears for missing Sydney teen who hasn’t been seen since leaving for hike on Wednesday",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/15/fears-for-missing-sydney-teen-who-hasnt-been-seen-since-leaving-for-hike-on-wednesday",
      "description": "<p>Fresh search teams to scour Nattai national park for Lily Hooper, 18, who failed to return home from a bushwalk</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The search for an 18-year-old bushwalker missing in the Southern Highlands of New South Wales since Wednesday is continuing, with fresh teams arriving at the Nattai national park on Saturday morning.</p><p>Lily Hooper left her home in Sydney’s south-west about 8am on 12 August, after telling family she was going for a hike in the national park, north-west of Mittagong.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/15/fears-for-missing-sydney-teen-who-hasnt-been-seen-since-leaving-for-hike-on-wednesday\">Continue reading...</a>",
